WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.653
- Social media is a
treasure trove of good news

00:00:02.653 --> 00:00:04.300
when you know where to look,

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.620
but you don't even have to look,

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.720
because I've got you covered.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.940
This is, "What I'm Liking".

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:08.773
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.773 --> 00:00:11.400
(audience cheers)

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.620
Anyone who has been here,

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.840
knows New York is one of
the most diverse cities

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:16.820
on the planet.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.920
It's what I love about it.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.220
In fact, people speak
more than 700 languages,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.600
across the five boroughs.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.790
That's crazy.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.520
Well, there's a New Yorker whose attempts

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.030
to learn some of those languages,

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.010
especially the more obscure ones,

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.470
have made him a viral
star, check this out.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.580
- And where are all these clothes from?

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.413
- Nigeria.

00:00:35.413 --> 00:00:38.214
- Nigeria? Oh.

00:00:38.214 --> 00:00:40.870
(man speaks Yoruba)

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:41.974
(lady laughs)

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:44.773
(lady speaks Yoruba)

00:00:44.773 --> 00:00:47.773
(man speaks Yoruba)

00:00:52.738 --> 00:00:54.213
- Oh American, yes.

00:00:54.213 --> 00:00:57.005
(man speaks Yoruba)

00:00:57.005 --> 00:01:00.172
(woman speaks Yoruba)

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.818
- Maybe like next week.

00:01:03.818 --> 00:01:05.963
- [Man In Black Tshirt] You try, you try.

00:01:05.963 --> 00:01:07.283
(audience cheers)

00:01:07.283 --> 00:01:09.931
- Say hello to Arieh Smith, y'all.

00:01:09.931 --> 00:01:12.630
(audience applauds)

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.510
I mean that was incredible.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:16.343
First of all,

00:01:16.343 --> 00:01:18.270
their reactions to you
speaking were incredible,

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.530
but you were speaking a
Nigerian language called,

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:21.363
is it Yoruba?

00:01:21.363 --> 00:01:22.196
- Yoruba. Yoruba.

00:01:22.196 --> 00:01:23.029
- Yoruba?

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.130
- With the tones Yoruba.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.200
- Yoruba, okay.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.380
And you were speaking that in the clips.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:29.320
So how many languages do you know?

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.980
- Yeah, so to be honest,

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.634
the languages that I speak
decently well probably only four.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.514
- Well, you lazy man.

00:01:36.514 --> 00:01:37.347
(audience laughs)

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:38.400
Only four.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.891
- Yes.

00:01:39.891 --> 00:01:43.313
So I speak English, Mandarin,
Cantonese and Spanish.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:46.510
But really over the past
year I've been studying,

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:51.510
you know, 15 or so languages
somewhat simultaneously.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:52.970
If you look at New York,

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.600
every neighborhood has its own little...

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.500
Like you have one neighborhood
that's like entirely African,

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.830
you have another neighborhood
that's like entirely Russian,

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:05.042
so learn these languages
and go down there,

00:02:05.042 --> 00:02:05.900
(Arieh coughs)

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.610
- What a way to connect with people.

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:09.370
- Yeah it's really incredible.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:12.580
I think it makes people feel
seen and I think it makes-

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.110
- [Kelly] It's shifting
the narrative. I like it.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:15.307
- Yeah.

00:02:15.307 --> 00:02:17.594
- Yeah. Thank you Arieh.

00:02:17.594 --> 00:02:19.231
- I really appreciate that,
I really do appreciate it.

00:02:19.231 --> 00:02:20.431
- It's so cool what you're doing.

00:02:20.431 --> 00:02:22.663
I'm liking your posts right now.

00:02:22.663 --> 00:02:24.631
And also this is our first
time ever doing this live.

00:02:24.631 --> 00:02:25.951
(audience cheers)

00:02:25.951 --> 00:02:29.160
So that's not all though, our
season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.820
the go to pen of The Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.030
thinks you're incredible, as we do,

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.480
So in recognition, they'd
like to write you a check

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.133
with their G2 gel ink pen
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:38.966
- What!

00:02:38.966 --> 00:02:40.087
- [Kelly] How's that sound?

00:02:40.087 --> 00:02:41.603
You make more videos!

00:02:41.603 --> 00:02:42.436
- Thank you

